    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d255">

                <pb facs="0327" n="211" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg211"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1070.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Sullivan.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-24T23:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 24, 1914, 11 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your February 21, 3 p.m. Your telegram will be laid before the President.</p>
                <p>To what extent have the alleged irregularities of Arias and Vidal interfered with
                    the fulfilment of the terms of the Convention? If evidence is such as to cause
                    Dominican Government to proclaim Arias or Vidal or both as offenders against the
                    law, how soon after such proclamation does Bordas believe constitutional
                    amendments and legislative reforms could be enacted and what would be the
                    character and extent of material assistance required by Constituted
                    Government?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
